{"format":1,"seq":144,"writes":[{"type":"document.change","id":2,"content":{"version":3,"kind":"delta","ops":[["p",["generation","message","content"],1,0,[{"type":"text","text":"I found the cause, and it was my fault. In the previous run (where you asked about grouping), one of my own git commands broke the run's conversation storage. The run then dropped your comment without saying so: no reply, no 😕 reaction, and the step still shows green. pi-action made it worse in two places, described below.\n\n## What happened, step by step (times from the job log)\n\n1. **07:20:57.** The run fetched `refs/pi/threads/46` at `5830d93` and continued the thread. New steps are committed to the local ref and pushed to origin in the background.\n\n2. **During the run.** To look at ear"}]],["a",["generation","message","content",0,"thinkingSignature"],""],["a",["generation","message","content",1,"text"],"lier sessions, I ran:\n   ```\n   git fetch origin '+refs/pi/*:refs/pi/*'\n   ```\n   The leading `+` forces the update, and the pattern covers `refs/pi/threads/46`, which is the ref the run was writing to. Origin still had `5830d93` because nothing had been pushed yet. So the fetch rewound the local ref and wiped out the steps committed in this run. That command was the mistake.\n\n3. **07:21:05.** The storage's next commit checks that the ref is where it left it before moving it (`updateRef` in `src/storage/git.ts`). It found `5830d93` instead, and pi-durable failed the whole session:\n   ```\n   ##[warning]Session failed after a storage error; close and reopen it\n   ```\n   My `bash` call was cut off mid-run, which is the `Tool bash was interrupted` I saw.\n\n4. **Your comment was silently dropped.** `ThreadConversation.track()` (`src/conversation.ts`) catches the error, logs it as that warning, and never delivers a result for the trigger. So no comment, no rocket or 😕 reaction (your comment only has 👀), and `Run pi-action` finished as **success**.\n\n5. **The save step gave a misleading warning.** The background sync pushed its last tip (`2b20a2c`). `src/push.ts` then read the rewound local ref (`5830d93`) and tried to push it. The push was rejected, with the message \"another writer moved it\". Really the local ref was *behind* origin, not on a different branch, and nothing was lost on origin. The warning is just wrong about the cause.\n\n## What I'd change\n\n| # | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Anything the agent runs (`git fetch`, `git update-ref`, `git gc --"]]}}]}